PROPOSAL v2 -- NOT APPLIED, NOT COMMITTED AS CODE. 2026-09-12, T26 lane.
Supersedes PROPOSAL_build_t26_registration_hook_NOT_APPLIED.diff, whose failure
mode 2 was WRONG and is corrected below.

=============================================================================
CORRECTION TO v2's OWN PREDECESSOR, FIRST, BECAUSE IT CHANGES THE DESIGN
=============================================================================
v1 said the certificate "does not pin the registration by sha256" and that
closing that would change the CERTIFICATE SCHEMA.  BOTH HALVES ARE WRONG.
`certify()` at build_t26.py:1625-1626 ALREADY writes

    "registration": {"path": os.path.relpath(registration or REGISTRATION),
                     "sha256": sha256_of(registration or REGISTRATION)},

and "registration" is already in CERT_REQUIRED.  THE FIELD EXISTS AND IS
POPULATED.  What does NOT happen is that `read_certificate()` never COMPARES it
to the live file: it checks `inputs_sha256`, the level, and the SURFACE sha
against the live registration, and walks straight past the registration sha it
is holding.  So THE SCHEMA DOES NOT CHANGE AT ALL -- the schema change I offered
to name in one line does not exist, and the fix is a comparison, not a field.

=============================================================================
WHAT v2 PROPOSES -- FOUR CHANGES, AND THEY ARE NOT SEPARABLE
=============================================================================
A one-flag hook is NOT sufficient: threading a path into readers that ignore it
produces a build whose ladder comes from one document and whose levels table
comes from another.  That is worse than no hook.

